+    /* FUNCTIONS OF ANOTHER BINARY LINKED INTO THE SAME MODULE
+     * (DOLRECOMP_EXTERNAL_RANGES=<file of "start end" hex pairs>).
+     *
+     * A call to an address outside this binary has no range, so the emitter
+     * cannot call it directly and exits to the runtime, which dispatches the
+     * callee and, when it returns, dispatches back: two trips through the
+     * host per call. A REL calls its DOL's SDK all the time - Twin Snakes'
+     * engine calls PSMTXMultVec, PSVECNormalize, GXSetArray thousands of
+     * times a frame (HANDOFF F386). When both are linked into one module
+     * the DOL's func_XXXXXXXX_budget symbols are there to call, so listed
+     * ranges are given to the emitter - and only to it: the dispatch header
+     * still describes this binary alone. */
